From ebf73aca347e241d79dbdd30af06ce5566b3d4aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SCARPxVeNOM <pratikkumar56778@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 07:48:17 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] perf(tor-js-wasm): reuse HTTP/1.1 connections per isolation
 key

Every request sent Connection: close, so each one paid for a new Tor
stream, TCP from the exit and a TLS handshake before the request left.
Keep connections and reuse them per isolation key, scheme, host and port:

- never across isolation keys, or between keyed and unkeyed requests;
- pooled only if the body ended exactly at its framed end (Content-Length,
  or chunked with its trailers read), the response wasn't HTTP/1.0 without
  keep-alive, and the server didn't send Connection: close;
- idle at most 30 s or just under the server's Keep-Alive timeout, retired
  2 min after opening; at most 4 idle per key and 32 in all, expired keys
  swept;
- a request whose reused connection closed before any response byte is sent
  once more on a new connection (RFC 9112 9.3.1); never after a timeout or
  a partial response, and streamed bodies always get a new connection.

Warm reads through 3 gateways, against the 0.4.4 worker: p50 827 -> 234 ms
(no key), 1,140 -> 203 ms (isolation key); 20 parallel reads 2.0 -> 1.0 s.
